  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Travel costs study visit on health infrastructure from Ukraine to the the Netherlands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports the logistics to implement a four (4) full-days study visit on rapid recovery of healthcare and infrastructure with focus on potential solutions where the Netherlands can be of added value. As result, twelve (12) representatives of Ukrainian government bodies, working on the recovery of healthcare infrastructure and policies will be part of this visit. This project enables that the members of the delegation, through showcasing, get practical understanding on how Dutch companies (active in the life sciences and health (LSH) and energy sector) can contribute to the recovery of the damaged healthcare infrastructure in Ukraine. Further, the visit will also facilitate the communication of the delegation with Dutch private and innovation organizations, which in the medium-long term can take part of rebuilding, repairing and modernising healthcare infrastructure (hospitals, rehabilitation centers, primary care), including design, turnkey solutions and medical logistics.</narrative>
  </description>
